<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/1fd6d3edf406> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "The Securities and Exchange Commission today announced settled charges against two investment advisers, Delphia (USA) Inc. and Global Predictions Inc., for making false and misleading statements about their purported use of artificial intelligence (AI)." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "3581" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/414b7b35bf52> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "The Securities and Exchange Commission today announced settled charges against two investment advisers, Delphia (USA) Inc. and Global Predictions Inc., for making false and misleading statements about their purported use of artificial intelligence (AI)." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "3581" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/6e0b7ff87dbb> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "2 investment advisers agreed to pay a total of $400,000 to settle charges by the Securities and Exchange Commission (SEC) the firms each engaged in artificial intelligence (AI) misrepresentations that misled clients about how they were using the technology." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "7585" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/7893aae3c335> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "After dismissing its lawsuit against the crypto exchange Coinbase in March, a second investigation into the exchange by the Securities and Exchange Commission has surfaced, according to a report from the New York Times." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "7585" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/8fffd35fdd2c> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "The U.S. Federal Trade Commission (FTC) took action against a pair of student loan debt relief companies for allegedly deceiving borrowers." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "7585" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/95846b7d87ce> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "The former chief executive officer of closed AI recruitment startup Joonko faces up to 40 years in prison and the potential of penalties levied by the Securities and Exchange Commission for allegedly defrauding investors of more than $27 million." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "7585" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/970b1be5190a> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "The Securities and Exchange Commission ordered the owner of Rimar Capital and a board member of its holding company to pay nearly $524,000 in penalties for defrauding investors with false and misleading statements about its use of artificial intelligence." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "7585" .

